ResumeScan

A free, browser-based tool that checks whether your CV is ATS-friendly. Paste your CV or upload a PDF/TXT file and get a score, a fix-first checklist and an optional keyword match against a job description.

Everything runs in the browser. Your CV is never uploaded or stored.

Features

	•	ATS score out of 100 with a prioritized fix list
	•	12+ checks: contact details, section headings, length, parser-unfriendly symbols, dates, action verbs, measurable results, weak phrases and buzzwords
	•	Keyword match against a pasted job description
	•	PDF and TXT upload (text extracted with pdf.js)
	•	"Check another CV" button that clears the CV, job description and file
	•	Responsive layout

Tech Stack

HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript in a single file. pdf.js is loaded from a CDN.

Run Locally

git clone https://github.com/nikhil-flux/resumescan.git
cd resumescan
python -m http.server 8000

Open http://127.0.0.1:8000/resumescan.html. You can also just double-click the file.

How It Works

	1.	Parse test: contact info, standard headings and symbols that confuse parsers
	2.	Quality test: length, action verbs, numbers and weak phrases
	3.	Keyword match: top keywords from the job post vs. your CV

Disclaimer

ResumeScan gives guidance, not a guarantee. Every ATS works differently, so use the score as an improvement checklist.

